{"id":"vfam","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":4,"of":16,"title":"Family and people","titleHe":"מִשְׁפָּחָה","goal":"Name everyone at the table — and notice which words come in gendered pairs.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Hebrew kinship terms almost all come in pairs: change the ending and you change the relative. Learn them two at a time."}],"vocab":[{"he":"אַבָּא","en":"dad","translit":"aba"},{"he":"אִמָּא","en":"mum","translit":"ima"},{"he":"אָב","en":"father","translit":"av"},{"he":"אֵם","en":"mother","translit":"em"},{"he":"הוֹרִים","en":"parents","translit":"horim"},{"he":"בֵּן","en":"son","translit":"ben"},{"he":"בַּת","en":"daughter","translit":"bat"},{"he":"אָח","en":"brother","translit":"ach"},{"he":"אָחוֹת","en":"sister","translit":"achot"},{"he":"סַבָּא","en":"grandfather","translit":"saba"},{"he":"סַבְתָּא","en":"grandmother","translit":"savta"},{"he":"נֶכֶד","en":"grandson","translit":"neched"},{"he":"נֶכְדָּה","en":"granddaughter","translit":"nechda"},{"he":"דּוֹד","en":"uncle","translit":"dod"},{"he":"דּוֹדָה","en":"aunt","translit":"doda"},{"he":"בֶּן דּוֹד","en":"cousin (m.)","translit":"ben dod"},{"he":"בַּעַל","en":"husband","translit":"ba'al"},{"he":"אִשָּׁה","en":"wife, woman","translit":"isha"},{"he":"חָתָן","en":"groom","translit":"chatan"},{"he":"כַּלָּה","en":"bride","translit":"kala"},{"he":"תִּינוֹק","en":"baby","translit":"tinok"},{"he":"נַעַר","en":"youth, boy","translit":"na'ar"},{"he":"זָקֵן","en":"old man, elder","translit":"zaken"},{"he":"שָׁכֵן","en":"neighbour","translit":"shachen"},{"he":"אוֹרֵחַ","en":"guest","translit":"oreach"},{"he":"יְלָדִים","en":"children","translit":"yeladim"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["thought","he said to him (Aramaic)","knee","dad"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אַבָּא","translit":"aba"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["tea","mum","but","pain"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אִמָּא","translit":"ima"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?